RANKINGS

OCRA National Rankings

The Obstacle Course Racing Association of Ireland (OCRA ÉIREANN) is working towards the development of a national ranking system for competitive obstacle racing in Ireland.

The aim of the rankings is to recognise consistent performance across approved competitions and create a stronger connection between individual races throughout the Irish OCR season.


Why National Rankings?

Obstacle racing in Ireland takes place across a variety of events and organisers.

A national ranking system can help connect these events into a wider competitive pathway and provide athletes with an opportunity to measure their performance across a season.

Rankings can also help:

- Recognise leading Irish athletes
- Encourage participation in multiple competitions
- Support athlete development
- Strengthen relationships between races
- Provide a clearer national competition structure
- Build a historical record of competitive performance


Ranking Events

Not every OCR event listed on the OCRA website will automatically contribute towards national rankings.

Only events specifically approved as OCRA Ranking Events will be eligible.

Potential Ranking Events may include:

- OCRA-organised events
- OCRA Sanctioned Events
- Irish National Championships
- OCRA Qualification Events
- Other approved competitive races

Approved events will be clearly identified as:

OCRA RANKING EVENT


Ranking Categories

Rankings may be maintained separately across different:

- Disciplines
- Categories
- Age Groups

This is intended to ensure that athletes are compared within appropriate competitive structures rather than forcing very different race formats into a single ranking.


Ranking Season

National rankings will operate over a defined competition season.

The ranking period, eligible events and scoring method will be published before an official ranking season begins.


How Ranking Points Will Work

OCRA is currently developing the ranking methodology.

The final system will be designed to reward competitive performance while remaining understandable and transparent for athletes.

The ranking rules will explain:

- Which events are eligible
- How points are awarded
- How many results count
- Whether National Championships receive additional weighting
- How ties are resolved
- Which categories are ranked


Rankings and Qualification

National rankings may potentially form part of future qualification or selection pathways.

However, a ranking position will only affect international qualification where this is specifically stated within the applicable qualification criteria.

Athletes should not assume that a national ranking automatically qualifies them for international competition.


Historical Rankings

Once an official ranking system is launched, final standings from each season should remain available permanently.

This will create a historical record of the development of competitive OCR in Ireland and recognise athletes who have led their categories over time.


National Rankings — Coming Soon

The full OCRA National Ranking system is currently being developed.

Details of the first ranking season, eligible competitions and points system will be published once the ranking structure has been finalised.


